    "description": "Angela Slobodyan is a journalist who survived 31 days of Russian captivity during the occupation of the Kherson region. She is travelling to The Hague to testify about the aggressor’s war crimes.  Combining telephone video evidence of the occupation, and interviews with survivors, Invasion is dedicated to Ukrainian acts of resistance. The women at the centre of the narrative not only demonstrated their heroism in resisting the occupiers, but also dared to give oral testimony about the unspeakable horrors they endured.  ",
